FFmpeg / FFprobe
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Bundled binaries: tools/ffmpeg/

The bundled build ships GNU GENERAL PUBLIC LICENSE Version 3 at:

    tools/ffmpeg/ffmpeg-8.1.1-essentials_build/LICENSE

This is the **GPL v3** build (the Gyan.dev "essentials" builds are configured
with --enable-gpl), not an LGPL build.

    ATTENTION — this affects how this application may be distributed.

GPL v3 is a strong copyleft license. Shipping these binaries inside a
distributable bundle can extend GPL obligations to the work as a whole,
depending on how the two are combined and distributed. Invoking ffmpeg.exe as a
separate process (which is what this application does — see runtime_tools.py)
is generally treated more favourably than linking, but bundling the GPL binary
in the same installer is a distribution of that binary and carries its own
requirements, including making the corresponding source available.

This has not been reviewed by a lawyer, and this file is not legal advice. For
commercial or closed-source distribution, the application provides built-in tools
in `runtime_tools.py` (`get_ffmpeg_license_info()`, `is_ffmpeg_lgpl()`):

  1. Dual-Distribution Support: The application resolves FFmpeg from PATH,
     environment variables (`CAPCUT_TOOL_FFMPEG`), or local folders. Distributors
     can ship without bundled binaries (unbundled mode) or supply LGPL-built binaries.
  2. LGPL Switch: To distribute with bundled FFmpeg legally under LGPL, replace
     the binaries with Gyan.dev or BtbN "shared-lgpl" builds (compiled without --enable-gpl).
  3. Source Availability: If distributing with GPL binaries, distribute the matching
     source code alongside the application bundle as mandated by GPL v3 section 6.

Upstream project: https://ffmpeg.org/
Bundled build:    Gyan.dev essentials, FFmpeg 8.1.1 (GPL v3 build)
Programmatic API: `runtime_tools.is_ffmpeg_lgpl()`


